---
import RootLayout from "../../layouts/RootLayout.astro";
---

<RootLayout title="Consulting — Chronopax" description="Cloud architecture, security infrastructure, and AI systems integration." width="md">
  <div class="page-header">
    <span class="eyebrow">Work with me</span>
    <h1>Consulting</h1>
  </div>

  <section class="intro-section">
    <h2>Let's build something worth building.</h2>
    <p>I work with organizations that need infrastructure done right — network
      architecture, cloud migrations, security design, and the hands-on delivery
      that makes sure it actually lands. Based in San Diego. Available for
      contract, project-based, and hourly engagements. Also available for
      longer-term arrangements when the work and fit make sense.</p>
    <p>If you need someone who can join a customer call, understand their network
      and applications, and translate that into a clear actionable design —
      reach out.</p>
    <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start a conversation →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="brings-section">
    <h2>What I bring</h2>
    <p>Technical depth from the physical layer up — hardware, cabling, routing,
      wireless, voice, video, cloud, and security. Pre-sales and solution
      engineering experience across carrier, enterprise, and SMB. Project
      delivery experience that includes the part where the construction timeline
      slips, the demarc moves, and someone has to fix it without losing the
      customer. Sales team enablement if you need your people to close more of
      the technical deals they're already sitting in front of.</p>
    <p>Started hands-on with computers and networks in the mid-1990s.
      Still hands-on today.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="focus-section">
    <h2>Areas of Focus</h2>
    <div class="accordion">

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">IP Transit &amp; BGP Architecture</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Designed and supported BGP-based connectivity at every level — from
            enterprise edge routing to carrier backbone architecture, working directly
            with ISPs, data centers, and global enterprise customers on path diversity,
            peering strategy, and traffic engineering. Backed by graduate-level
            networking coursework and hands-on CLI work across Cisco, Juniper, and
            open-source routing platforms.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: BGP design and review, edge routing architecture,
            peering and transit strategy, routing policy audits, and technical
            discovery for organizations evaluating their connectivity options or
            cleaning up someone else's design.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">SD-WAN &amp; WAN Design</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Designed and deployed SD-WAN architectures including rapid-deployment
            overlays, hybrid MPLS migrations, and multi-site DIA integration across
            carrier and enterprise environments. Continued designing WAN solutions
            through multiple roles and active certification work.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: SD-WAN design and vendor evaluation, MPLS migration
            planning, multi-site WAN architecture, hybrid connectivity design, and
            hands-on involvement through delivery.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">DDoS Mitigation &amp; Traffic Engineering</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Led technical discovery sessions with enterprise and carrier customers on
            DDoS requirements, scrubbing center design, black-hole routing, and traffic
            path diversity. Understand the full range of options from null-routing and
            ACLs to upstream scrubbing and BGP community-based mitigation, and how to
            match the right approach to the actual risk tolerance and budget of the
            organization.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: DDoS architecture review, mitigation strategy,
            scrubbing center evaluation, traffic engineering for resiliency, and
            practical advice on what level of protection actually makes sense for
            your environment.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Wireless &amp; RF Design</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Designed wireless systems from the ground up across hospitality, enterprise,
            venues, campgrounds, and multi-tenant buildings. RF surveys, heatmapping,
            channel planning, outdoor AP deployment, and LTE/wireless backhaul design
            going back to early carrier work where creative solutions included dual-LTE
            Yagi antenna architectures for remote environments with no wired options.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Wireless system design, RF surveys and heatmapping,
            outdoor and venue coverage, LTE/wireless backhaul planning, and
            troubleshooting existing deployments with poor coverage or interference.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Hospitality, Venue &amp; Multi-Tenant Networks</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Designed and delivered full-property network solutions for major hotel
            brands including managed Wi-Fi, SIP/PRI voice, security cameras, guest
            authentication, cabling, and redundant connectivity. Extended that work to
            venues, campgrounds, trailer parks, and multi-tenant buildings. Understand
            brand compliance requirements, property management system integration, and
            the constraints of working inside an operating property without disrupting
            guests or operations.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Full property network design, technology audits,
            managed service scoping, vendor coordination, and architecture that accounts
            for how the property actually operates.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Cloud Migration &amp; Architecture</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Started working on cloud connectivity designing AWS Direct Connect and
            Azure ExpressRoute solutions for enterprise customers, and pushed deeper
            through Azure certification, active AWS certification work, and hands-on
            project delivery. Have worked with organizations on cloud migration strategy,
            hybrid WAN design, and multi-cloud environments including legacy workloads
            that need to coexist with modern infrastructure. Understand the difference between a migration done right and one
            that just moves the problem somewhere more expensive.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Cloud migration planning and architecture review,
            hybrid connectivity design, multi-cloud strategy, cloud cost optimization
            assessment, and technical advisory for organizations evaluating or
            recovering from a cloud migration.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Low-Latency &amp; Redundant Network Design</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Designed and supported low-latency connectivity solutions for financial
            and gaming clients throughout my career — from last-mile selection and
            route optimization to redundancy planning at the transport and application
            layer. Know how to design a network around a budget and a risk tolerance:
            maybe everything fails except the front desk, or the register keeps working
            but streaming goes dark, or you black-hole traffic to protect the core
            while one path recovers. Practical resilience, not just theoretical.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Low-latency connectivity design, redundancy planning,
            failover architecture, last-mile evaluation, and helping organizations
            define what "always on" actually needs to mean for their specific situation.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Voice &amp; UCaaS</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Supported voice infrastructure across every role — SIP trunking, PRI,
            hosted voice, and UCaaS platform integration. Designed SIP/PRI systems
            for hospitality properties and supported voice connectivity and architecture
            throughout carrier and enterprise work. Deeply familiar with the network
            requirements that make voice work reliably even if the underlying platform
            changes.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Voice connectivity design, SIP/PRI scoping, network
            readiness assessment for UCaaS migrations, and troubleshooting voice
            quality issues at the network layer.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Network Security &amp; Segmentation</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Incorporated security into network design throughout my career — firewall
            placement, VLAN segmentation, guest network isolation, managed firewall
            recommendations, and security camera network design. Graduate-level
            security training applied to practical recommendations for regulated
            industries. Understand how to layer security without destroying performance
            or making the network unmanageable.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Security architecture review, segmentation design,
            firewall placement and policy recommendations, and practical security
            improvements that don't require a full rip-and-replace.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Technical Sales Enablement</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Trained and coached sales teams across multiple organizations covering
            technical fundamentals, qualifying the right opportunities, understanding
            customer environments, and translating complex architecture into language
            that closes deals. Built playbooks, ran workshops, and joined customer
            calls to validate designs and raise team close rates across fiber,
            wireless, carrier, enterprise, and cloud products.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Sales team technical training, pre-sales process
            design, qualification framework development, joint customer calls, and
            helping your sales organization win the deals that require someone who
            actually understands the network.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion-item">
        <summary class="accordion-summary">
          <span class="accordion-title">Hardware, Infrastructure &amp; Systems Management</span>
          <span class="accordion-chevron">&#8250;</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-content">
          <p>Started hands-on with computers and networks in the mid-1990s through a
            computer repair program — building, troubleshooting, and understanding
            systems before managed services abstracted most of it away. That foundation
            carried through every role since. On the network hardware side: rack design,
            cabling, switch configuration, router deployment, firewall installation, and
            physical infrastructure documentation across carrier, enterprise, hospitality,
            and data center environments. On the systems side: Windows Server, Linux
            (since 2008), virtualization, and the management plane that keeps
            infrastructure observable — monitoring, patching, logging, and the tooling
            that tells you something is wrong before the customer calls.</p>
          <p>What I can do for you: Hardware selection and scoping, rack and
            infrastructure design, network equipment configuration and deployment,
            systems management architecture, and the practical hands-on work that
            makes a design actually land in the real world.</p>
        </div>
      </details>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="opportunity-section">
    <h2>Open to the right opportunity</h2>
    <p>Beyond project work, I'm selectively open to full-time roles where the
      work is genuinely interesting and the compensation reflects the level.
      If that sounds like your organization — LinkedIn is the best place
      to start.</p>
    <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/burleyjoe/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Connect on LinkedIn →</a>
  </section>

  <section class="support-section">
    <h2>Support the work</h2>
    <p>Interested in supporting ongoing open source projects?</p>
    <a href="https://patreon.com/Chronopax" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline">Support on Patreon →</a>
  </section>
</RootLayout>

<style lang="scss">
  .page-header {
    margin: 3rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: block;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-accent-teal);
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .intro-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);

    p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 600px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }

    .btn-primary {
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  .brings-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);

    p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 600px;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
  }

  .focus-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  /* Accordion */
  .accordion {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .accordion-item {
    background: var(--color-bg-card);
    border: 0.5px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-left-color 0.2s;

    &[open] {
      border-left-color: var(--color-accent-teal);
    }

    &:hover:not([open]) > .accordion-summary {
      border-left-color: var(--color-accent-orange);
    }
  }

  .accordion-summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.85rem 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    user-select: none;

    &::-webkit-details-marker {
      display: none;
    }
  }

  .accordion-title {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .accordion-chevron {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  details[open] .accordion-chevron {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  .accordion-content {
    padding: 0 1rem 1rem;

    p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;

      &:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
      }
    }
  }

  .opportunity-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);

    p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      max-width: 600px;
      margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
  }

  .support-section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;

    p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
  }

  .text-link {
    color: var(--color-accent-orange);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 0.9rem;

    &:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s;

    &.btn-primary {
      background: var(--color-accent-orange);
      color: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--color-accent-orange);

      &:hover {
        background: var(--color-accent-orange-dark);
        border-color: var(--color-accent-orange-dark);
      }
    }

    &.btn-outline {
      background: transparent;
      color: var(--color-text-primary);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border-hover);

      &:hover {
        border-color: var(--color-accent-orange);
        color: var(--color-accent-orange);
      }
    }
  }
</style>
